","G2316","N-GSM-T","of God"],["καὶ","kai","G2532","CONJ","and"],["διδάσκων","didaskōn","G1321","V-PAP-NSM","teaching"],["τὰ","ta","G3588","T-APN","the [things]"],["περὶ","peri","G4012","PREP","concerning"],["τοῦ","tou","G3588","T-GSM","the"],["κυρίου","kuriou","G2962","N-GSM-T","Lord"],["Ἰησοῦ","Iēsou","G2424","N-GSM-P","Jesus"],["Χριστοῦ","Christou","G5547","N-GSM-T","Christ"],["μετὰ","meta","G3326","PREP","with"],["πάσης","pasēs","G3956","A-GSF","all"],["παρρησίας","parrēsias","G3954","N-GSF","boldness"],["ἀκωλύτως","akōlutōs","G209","ADV","unhinderedly"]],"x":[[44004029,44004029,10],[49006019,49006020,10],[40004023,40004023,8],[44028023,44028023,8],[44008012,44008012,7],[44020025,44020025,7],[50001014,50001014,7],[55004017,55004017,7],[44004031,44004031,6],[44005042,44005042,5]],"xn":15}},"people":[{"id":"paul_2479","name":"Paul","also":"Saul, Mercurius","summary":"Saul was born about the same time as our Lord. His circumcision-name was Saul, and probably the name Paul was also given to him in infancy “for use in the Gentile world,” as “Saul” would be his Hebrew home-name.","verses":179,"father":"","mother":"","v":[3,8,15,16,17,25,30]},{"id":"publius_2374","name":"Publius","also":"","summary":"“the chief man of the island” of Malta (Acts 28:7), who courteously entertained Paul and his shipwrecked companions for three days, till they found a more permanent place of residence; for they remained on the island for three months, till the stormy season had passed.","verses":2,"father":"","mother":"","v":[7,8]},{"id":"jesus_905","name":"Jesus","also":"Immanuel, Emmanuel, Messiah, Shiloh, Christ, Jesus Christ, Messias","summary":"Anointed, the Greek translation of the Hebrew word rendered “Messiah”, the official title of our Lord, occurring five hundred and fourteen times in the New Testament.","verses":1831,"father":"Joseph","mother":"Mary","v":[23,31]},{"id":"moses_2108","name":"Moses","also":"","summary":"Drawn (or Egypt. mesu, “son;” hence Rameses, royal son). On the invitation of Pharaoh (Gen. 45:17-25), Jacob and his sons went down into Egypt.","verses":774,"father":"Amram","mother":"Jochebed","v":[23]},{"id":"holy_spirit_7400","name":"Holy Spirit","also":"Comforter, Holy Ghost","summary":"The third Person of the adorable Trinity.","verses":246,"father":"","mother":"","v":[25]},{"id":"isaiah_617","name":"Isaiah","also":"Esaias","summary":"The son of Amoz (Isa. 1:1; 2:1), who was apparently a man of humble rank. His wife was called “the prophetess” (8:3), either because she was endowed with the prophetic gift, like Deborah (Judg. 4:4) and Huldah (2 Kings 22:14-20), or simply because she was the wife of “the prophet” (Isa. 38:1).","verses":53,"father":"Amoz","mother":"","v":[25]}],"places":[{"id":"melita_761","name":"Melita","kind":"Island","lat":35.87374,"lon":14.44874,"summary":"(Acts 27:28), an island in the Mediterranean, the modern Malta. Here the ship in which Paul was being conveyed a prisoner to Rome was wrecked.","verses":1,"v":[1]},{"id":"alexandria_46","name":"Alexandria","kind":"City","lat":31.19537,"lon":29.90413,"summary":"The ancient metropolis of Lower Egypt, so called from its founder, Alexander the Great (about B.C. 333). It was for a long period the greatest of existing cities, for both Nineveh and Babylon had been destroyed, and Rome had not yet risen to greatness.","verses":3,"v":[11]},{"id":"syracuse_1121","name":"Syracuse","kind":"City","lat":37.05963,"lon":15.29382,"summary":"A city on the south-east coast of Sicily, where Paul landed and remained three days when on his way to Rome (Acts 28:12). It was distinguished for its magnitude and splendour.","verses":1,"v":[12]},{"id":"puteoli_963","name":"Puteoli","kind":"City","lat":40.82796,"lon":14.12187,"summary":"A city on the coast of Campania, on the north shore of a bay running north from the Bay of Naples, at which Paul landed on his way to Rome, from which it was distant 170 miles.","verses":1,"v":[13]},{"id":"rhegium_999","name":"Rhegium","kind":"City","lat":38.11115,"lon":15.64924,"summary":"Breach, a town in the south of Italy, on the Strait of Messina, at which Paul touched on his way to Rome (Acts 28:13).","verses":1,"v":[13]},{"id":"rome_1013","name":"Rome","kind":"City","lat":41.89262,"lon":12.48435,"summary":"The most celebrated city in the world at the time of Christ. It is said to have been founded B.C. 753. When the New Testament was written, Rome was enriched and adorned with the spoils of the world, and contained a population estimated at 1,200,000, of which the half were slaves, and including representatives of nearly every nation then known.","verses":9,"v":[14,16]},{"id":"appii_forum_427","name":"Appii forum","kind":"Landmark","lat":41.46801,"lon":12.99372,"summary":"I.e., “the market of Appius” (Acts 28:15, R.V.), a town on the road, the “Appian Way,” from Rome to Brundusium. It was 43 miles from Rome. Here Paul was met by some Roman Christians on his way to the capital.","verses":1,"v":[15]},{"id":"three_taverns_1159","name":"Three Taverns","kind":"Landmark","lat":41.59132,"lon":12.82864,"summary":"A place on the great “Appian Way,” about 11 miles from Rome, designed for the reception of travellers, as the name indicates. Here Paul, on his way to Rome, was met by a band of Roman Christians (Acts 28:15).","verses":1,"v":[15]},{"id":"jerusalem_636","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"City","lat":31.77667,"lon":35.23417,"summary":"Called also Salem, Ariel, Jebus, the “city of God,” the “holy city;” by the modern Arabs el-Khuds, meaning “the holy;” once “the city of Judah” (2 Chr. 25:28).","verses":754,"v":[17]},{"id":"judea_657","name":"Judea","kind":"Region","lat":31.77744,"lon":35.23494,"summary":"After the Captivity this name was applied to the whole of the country west of the Jordan (Hag. 1:1, 14; 2:2).","verses":44,"v":[21]}],"events":[{"id":"paul_s_journey_to_rome_381","title":"Paul's Journey to Rome","year":56,"summary":"Passage: Acts 27:1–28:31. People: Paul, Luke, Aristarchus, Julius. Place: Pheni